{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-34:000001:issue_created:bob-cli-34:487d57153bc9212148d3cf4d837fdc93d36cb9dc3c3fddc0d581a5c40073ae28","timestamp":"2026-10-01T03:56:47Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.0um","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"bob-cli-34","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"bob-cli-34","title":"Priority roll decay: Ctrl+Enter takes the recommended roll","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-10-01T03:56:47Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.0um","updated_at":"2026-10-01T03:56:47Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"In the Ctrl+Shift+P picker, Ctrl+Enter on `scheduled` takes the recommended roll in one keypress, and the date it will write is shown on the `scheduled` row. The roll follows a configurable decay ladder read from the task's Schedule Log. A level is re-rolled `rolls` times (default 1), the next recommended roll moves the task one level down (P2 → P3), and past the last level it cancels the task. This works for single tasks, `^prj` tasks, counted sessions and Task Link sessions, and every write is a guarded, logged, one-undo edit.","design":"plan:202609/priority_roll_decay.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202609/priority_roll_decay.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
